# tokyo-night — Tokyo Night (Storm), mapped onto Ergon's 22 roles.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/enkia/tokyo-night-vscode-theme
# Licence:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2018-present Enkia
#
# Storm, not Night: Storm's ground (#24283B) has enough lift off black that the
# raised surfaces stay distinguishable, which matters here because Ergon uses
# three background steps and Night compresses them.
#
# COOL_DIMMER is #5F6996, Storm's actual comment colour. The widely-copied
# #565F89 is wrong for Storm -- it appears in older tables and in Night-derived
# ports, and was caught by checking the published theme rather than a summary.

# -- neutrals ---------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_BG0=#24283B          # bg
COOL_BG1=#292E42          # bg_highlight
COOL_BG2=#414868          # black, the border step
COOL_FG0=#C0CAF5          # variables / primary text
COOL_FG1=#A9B1D6          # editor foreground
COOL_DIM=#8089B3          # terminal foreground
COOL_DIMMER=#5F6996       # comment
# -- the ramp: cyan -> blue -> magenta -> orange -> red ---------------------
COOL_0=#7DCFFF
COOL_1=#7AA2F7
COOL_2=#BB9AF7
COOL_3=#FF9E64
COOL_4=#F7768E
# -- alert pair -------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_HOT_0=#2AC3DE        # cyan
COOL_HOT_4=#F7768E        # red
# -- off-ramp tints ---------------------------------------------------------
COOL_MINT=#73DACA         # terminal green
COOL_BLUSH=#BB9AF7        # magenta
# -- semantic aliases -------------------------------------------------------
COOL_ACCENT=#7AA2F7       # blue
COOL_ACTIVE=#BB9AF7       # magenta
COOL_URGENT=#F7768E       # red
COOL_WARN=#E0AF68         # yellow
COOL_GOOD=#9ECE6A         # green
COOL_INACTIVE=#414868
